L001757	As previously noted, the first three moments of $\bra{\psi}E^\dagger E\ket{\psi}$ are independent of $M$ and depend solely on the specific form of $E$. Therefore, the relationship between kurtosis and $M$ is reflected solely in the fourth moment, allowing us to derive Theorem \ref{theo:formerkurtosis}.
L001758	\begin{theorem}\label{theo:formerkurtosis}
L001759	    The set of all states with the same magic $M$ exhibits a decrease in the kurtosis of Trotter error $\bra{\psi}E^\dagger E\ket{\psi}$ as the magic increases. Specifically, the kurtosis satisfies:
L001760	    \begin{equation*}
L001761	        \mathop{\mathrm{Kur}}_{\ket{\psi}\sim\cM(\psi_0)}\left(\bra{\psi}E^\dagger E\ket{\psi}\right)=\alpha +\beta M\ge0
L001762	    \end{equation*}
L001763	    where $\alpha,\beta$ are some constants related to $E$, and $\beta<0$ when $n$ is large.
L001764	\end{theorem}
L001765	\begin{proof}
